Answer: If you mean an arbitrary filter that matches a `goal` string, then you can't do it. Although the SQL statement looks like a parametric one, it is actually a `case` statement, which can only match a single `value` for each row.

You will need to handle this in your code.

\begin{code}
Select * from users where goal not like '%write a post%'
\end{code}

This may not be the most elegant method, but it should get you started on your own.

